1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,699
Form C is the core offering filing
for a Reg CF raise.

2
00:00:03,699 --> 00:00:07,380
It is not a prospectus reviewed
and approved by the SEC.

3
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:11,521
Use it as a structured map of the
company, security, and risks.

4
00:00:11,521 --> 00:00:15,184
Start with the business
description and team, then read

5
00:00:15,184 --> 00:00:19,114
the target and maximum raise,
deadline, price or conversion

6
00:00:19,114 --> 00:00:21,511
terms, and intended use of
proceeds.

7
00:00:21,511 --> 00:00:25,224
Check the capitalization section
to see who already owns

8
00:00:25,224 --> 00:00:29,136
securities and whether other
instruments may convert later.

9
00:00:29,136 --> 00:00:32,534
Review related-party
transactions and the financial

10
00:00:32,534 --> 00:00:36,731
statements, paying attention to
their date and whether they are

11
00:00:36,731 --> 00:00:38,863
certified, reviewed, or audited.

12
00:00:38,863 --> 00:00:43,052
Then read the risk factors and
any attached exhibits, including

13
00:00:43,052 --> 00:00:44,582
the security agreement.

14
00:00:44,582 --> 00:00:48,920
Look for differences between the
short pitch and the formal terms.

15
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:52,770
A company could raise less than
its maximum, or the use of

16
00:00:52,770 --> 00:00:55,624
proceeds could depend on the
amount raised.

17
00:00:55,624 --> 00:00:59,945
The filing gives information to
analyze; it does not certify that

18
00:00:59,945 --> 00:01:01,408
the business is sound.

19
00:01:01,408 --> 00:01:03,393
If a crucial term is unclear,

20
00:01:03,393 --> 00:01:06,816
pause and seek qualified advice
before committing.

